<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran's Red Crescent says twenty-three days of American and Israeli strikes have damaged eighty-one thousand homes, along with hospitals, schools, and ambulances across the country.</s> <s>President Trump rejected a formal ceasefire yesterday but promised to wind down operations — a pledge made without a timeline and without the congressional authorization that Democrats are now demanding under the War Powers Act.</s> <s>No ceasefire is in place, the Red Crescent has called for an emergency international response, and the strikes continue into their fourth week.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A drone struck <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛl dɑːˈeɪn">el-Daein</phoneme> Teaching Hospital on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːd æl ˈfɪt.ər">Eid al-Fitr</phoneme>, killing sixty-four people in one of Sudan's last functioning medical facilities.</s> <s>The World Health Organization has documented more than two thousand deaths in over two hundred attacks on healthcare since the civil war began in April twenty twenty-three — a conflict the United Nations calls the world's largest humanitarian crisis.</s> <s>The hospital can no longer function, and the organization that counted the dead has no power to stop the next strike.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel's defense minister ordered Lebanese border villages leveled — in his words, like Gaza — a plan that would prevent one million displaced Lebanese from returning home.</s> <s>The military also intends to destroy the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kæsˈmiː.jə">Qasmiyeh</phoneme> Bridge near <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɔːr">Tyre</phoneme>, severing the city from the rest of the country.</s> <s>What began as a military campaign now carries the architecture of permanent displacement, with demolition as stated policy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Observers in Congo-Brazzaville say the biometric voting devices the government purchased as democratic infrastructure came pre-loaded with results.</s> <s>President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="dəˈniː">Denis</phoneme> <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="sæˈsuː ŋˈɡɛ.soʊ">Sassou-Nguesso</phoneme>, who has held power for forty of the last forty-seven years, was declared the winner with just under ninety-five percent of the vote.</s> <s>Civil society has filed a legal challenge, but no court has ever overturned an election in a country where the judiciary answers to the president.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uganda's leading opposition figure <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈboʊ.bi">Bobi</phoneme> Wine fled the country and surfaced at the United States Capitol, saying he feared for his life.</s> <s>Wine lost the twenty twenty-one presidential election to <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈjɒ.wɛ.ri muːˈsɛv.ən.i">Yoweri Museveni</phoneme>, who has held power since nineteen eighty-six and has systematically dismantled every institutional check on his authority.</s> <s>His departure leaves Uganda's opposition without its most visible leader inside the country at the moment it needs one most.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Thirty-three heads of state in the Community of Latin American and Caribbean States demanded an immediate ceasefire in the war between the United States and Iran.</s> <s>The bloc — the first major regional grouping to formally oppose the conflict — heard Colombian President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɡuːˈstɑː.voʊ ˈpɛ.troʊ">Gustavo Petro</phoneme> warn that the strikes risk triggering a global financial crisis.</s> <s>The declaration marks a degree of hemispheric unity against Washington not seen in decades.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Slovenians vote today on whether to reverse their recognition of Palestinian statehood.</s> <s>Former prime minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈjɑː.nɛz ˈjɑːn.ʃɑː">Janez Janša</phoneme> has pledged to revoke recognition and end cooperation with the International Criminal Court if he wins.</s> <s>A <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈjɑːn.ʃɑː">Janša</phoneme> victory would make Slovenia the first European Union member to reverse Palestinian recognition — a signal other right-leaning European governments would study closely.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indigenous leaders from across the Amazon gathered in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="brɑːˈziːl.jə">Brasília</phoneme> to reject Western portrayals that cast them as passive guardians of nature.</s> <s>Those portrayals have shaped land policy for decades, stripping communities of real authority over a biome covering forty percent of South America.</s> <s>The leaders demanded legal control over their own territories — not symbolic roles in someone else's environmental narrative.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Qatari military helicopter crashed in the Persian Gulf, killing all six people aboard.</s> <s>Qatar hosts <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="æl uːˈdeɪd">Al Udeid</phoneme> Air Base, the largest American military installation in the region, in a Gulf that has been under Iranian blockade for four weeks.</s> <s>Whether the crash resulted from hostile fire or mechanical failure remains unconfirmed, and that ambiguity itself measures the tension now running through the waterway.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Indonesian President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="prɑːˈboʊ.woʊ suːbiˈɑːn.toʊ">Prabowo Subianto</phoneme> is targeting eight percent economic growth — a rate the country has not achieved since the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="suːˈhɑːr.toʊ">Suharto</phoneme> era.</s> <s>His plan rests on thirty thousand school kitchens, eighty thousand village cooperatives, and one million new homes to drive domestic demand from the bottom up.</s> <s>The government's own first-quarter projection is five point five percent, and no one in Jakarta has explained how to close that gap.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea agreed on a sixteen point six billion dollar emergency budget as the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hɔːrˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme> blockade drove the won past fifteen hundred to the dollar.</s> <s>The country imports nearly all its oil, and the crisis has demonstrated how quickly a distant naval blockade can destabilize an advanced industrial economy.</s> <s>The National Assembly votes on the package April tenth — if it fails, the government has no fallback plan to absorb the oil shock.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kenya now spends one billion dollars a year servicing the Chinese loans that built its Standard Gauge Railway.</s> <s>China constructed the line between twenty thirteen and twenty nineteen with a regional network in mind, but has refused to extend further credit until Kenya clears its existing debt.</s> <s>The railway was supposed to connect East Africa — instead, it reaches a wall of compounding interest.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Beijing is subsidizing one-person companies built on artificial intelligence platforms, a direct response to an economy producing eleven million university graduates a year without enough jobs to absorb them.</s> <s>A single entrepreneur using AI agents can now perform work that once required entire teams, and the program has no stated enrollment cap.</s> <s>No one has answered whether AI micro-firms can absorb structural unemployment or merely disguise it.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Medicare's chief administrator admitted that TrumpRx — the president's drug-pricing executive order — covers only uninsured patients who pay cash, leaving two hundred million insured Americans entirely unaffected.</s> <s>The admission quietly undercuts months of promises that the order would lower costs broadly.</s> <s>Millions of insured Americans will keep paying full price unless Congress legislates what the executive order never actually delivered.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>School phone bans now cover more than half the world's countries, spanning every income level on every continent.</s> <s>UNESCO found the prohibitions spread in under three years, driven by mounting evidence linking smartphone use in classrooms to lower test scores and rising anxiety.</s> <s>The agency urged remaining countries to act before the next academic year — a rare case where global policy is outpacing the technology it aims to regulate.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>